WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:02.120
Hi everyone, my name is Sai Vennam

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.760
and I'm with the IBM Cloud team.

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:07.500
Today let's talk about Red Hat OpenShift on IBM Cloud.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.980
First, we'll introduce OpenShift.

00:00:09.980 --> 00:00:13.220
OpenShift is an open source application platform

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:16.100
based on Kubernetes and container technology.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.240
It focuses on making the Kubernetes experience easier

00:00:19.240 --> 00:00:21.980
for developers, as well as operations teams.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:24.700
Red Hat OpenShift on IBM Cloud allows you

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.540
to focus on managing and developing your application.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.400
Let us take care of the heavy lifting with the infrastructure,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.200
allowing you to create a highly available

00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:36.430
and managed OpenShift cluster with the click of a button.

00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:40.640
Together, OpenShift and IBM Cloud Kubernetes Service is a perfect match,

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.380
providing you with an industry-leading developer experience.

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.980
For one, you will get automated provisioning,

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.420
updates and patching,

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:51.480
as well as 24/7 global support.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.700
Currently we manage over 14,000 production clusters

00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:56.760
in IBM Cloud Kubernetes Service.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:01:00.780
In addition, you can resiliency and security across the board.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:02.840
Take advantage of highly available masters

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:04.520
to administer your clusters

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:07.960
and use options for dedicated computing resources and bare metal.

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.820
With multizone regions,

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.260
you get stability across data centers

00:01:12.260 --> 00:01:14.780
- further enhancing your  HA story.

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:18.060
On the security front, you get compliance out-of-the-box

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:20.260
with things like HIPAA and GDPR.

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.440
Finally, you get push-button integrations

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.760
with the entire suite of IBM and Red Hat middleware.

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:27.460
Build beyond those basics,

00:01:27.460 --> 00:01:30.220
and start taking advantage of high value services,

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:32.880
like AI and Hyperledger capabilities.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.660
With Red Hat and IBM together,

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:38.060
we're building out a unified open hybrid cloud platform.

00:01:38.060 --> 00:01:40.560
Whether you're running on-premises, or in the cloud,

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:43.140
taking advantage of Kubernetes, OpenShift,

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:45.380
serverless, or CF technology,

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.940
IBM Cloud is unifying these choices

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.560
and bringing them under one management platform

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.380
powered by open container technologies.

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.440
With the unified Red Hat and IBM Cloud platform,

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:00.140
start planning your open hybrid cloud strategy today.

